 ('9c40c447-c028-5b75-abce-20786e52eb82', '2026-2027', 9690, 18000, 18780, 740, 11950, 1250, 'merit_only', false, true, 693, 6435, false, true, 'CDS G1 (30 credit hours): in-state $323/credit, nonresident $600/credit. tuition_intl_usd = 30 x the $626 international per-credit rate on the A-State international tuition page (which adds a $350 per-term international fee, a $50 application fee, a $280 health-screening fee and $570-650/semester required health insurance; its own 2026-27 undergraduate estimate is $29,646 for a 12-credit year including dorm room and board). H6: only institutional non-need-based aid for nonresidents; 693 nonresidents received it (average $6,435).; A-State''s international freshman scholarship is $3,000 per year (also $3,000 for transfers with 24+ hours); it requires full admission, a 3.25 GPA and English proficiency, and cannot be combined with other scholarships. International students are not eligible for federal aid; CDS H6 reports only non-need-based institutional aid for nonresidents (693 recipients, average $6,435).', '25ace5ed-8043-5904-9bcf-0506d4e2fa31');
