 ('ac92fb49-45d0-5adb-b5b1-e81459c44faa', '2026-2027', 12988, 18510, 22457, 16800, 800, 7093, 47150, false, 'CSU''s international planning estimate for a bachelor''s student (page does not state the year; assumed 2026-27): tuition and fees $22,457, room and meals $16,800, books $800, health insurance $3,523, local transportation $1,770 and personal expenses $1,800 (other = $7,093); total $47,150. Extra fees: $100 one-time international matriculation fee and $30 per semester international services fee. The CSU Guarantee locks tuition for four years.; College Navigator estimated expenses for full-time beginning undergraduates, 2024-25 (tuition and fees; on-campus food and housing).; No international-specific scholarship is published. CSU''s automatic freshman merit scholarships ($2,000-$7,000 per year) and the CLE Gateway Grant are restricted to U.S. citizens and permanent residents, and the international scholarship page only links to outside resources. Treat aid for international freshmen as unconfirmed.', 'b1cd8c83-ad20-5c13-9c8d-353d249cacd8');
