 ('ff88d87f-2080-5255-91cf-71645b8f2cb1', '2026-2027', 10278, 31068, 31068, 160, 13610, 1200, 6900, 52938, 'merit_only', false, true, false, 'Official COA page, full-time undergraduate: out-of-state tuition $31,068 (12 hours x $1,294.50 x 2 terms; in-state $10,278), capital improvements fee $100 and activity fee $60, housing estimate $8,030 (UM housing ranges $6,134-$16,000) and food $5,580, books $1,200, personal $3,500, travel $3,400 (other_usd = personal + travel); out-of-state total $52,938. International students pay the non-resident rate.; International Academic Excellence scholarships are automatic on admission (no separate application), by US-scale GPA, for 4 years: Mississippi Premier $28,893/yr (3.9-4.0; max 20 awardees per country per year, in order of admission), Champion $12,000 (3.75-3.89), Magnolia $9,500 (3.5-3.74), Legacy $5,000 (3.25-3.49). Separate SAT/ACT scholarships (from $3,000 up to $15,000 at the 3.0-3.49 GPA tier, rising with score) cannot be stacked with them. Need-based aid for internationals is not mentioned.', 'f19898bc-4df9-52d1-b98c-292cd314e00f');
