 ('720ca07a-12a9-5a94-b4f8-0b86eb412882', '2026-2027', 6838, 20968, 20968, 1986, 23890, 1100, 4362, 52306, 'none', false, false, false, 'Computed from SF State''s 2026-27 budget (on campus): tuition $6,838, mandatory fees $1,986, housing $18,270 plus food $5,620, books $1,100, transportation $1,566 plus personal $2,796 (loan fee $62 left out), plus the nonresident/international charge of $471 per unit for an assumed 30 units ($14,130). SF State''s own on-campus total is $38,238 before that charge. International students must also buy health insurance (cost not found).; SF State''s Office of International Programs says there is no U.S. financial aid or international student scholarships to cover international students'' studies at SF State. Applicants below the TOEFL/IELTS minimum may enroll in SF State''s American Language Institute (intensive English; ali.sfsu.edu), which issues visa documents; the page does not call it conditional admission.', '624724da-2916-58cf-b17a-f20684210a89');
